{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevStripGrowthBoxReduction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevStripGrowthBoxReduction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Basis.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Basis.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Complex.Basic","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.DoublyPeriodicLiouville"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevStripGrowthBoxReduction.comparable_of_periodic_ballBound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevStripGrowthBoxReduction.comparable_of_periodic_ballBound","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FaddeevStripGrowthBoxReduction.lean#L89-L130","doc":"**Two-sided (comparability) form.** If the ratio `r` is doubly-periodic and both\n`‖r‖ ≤ C` and `1/C ≤ ‖r‖` hold on the fundamental ball, they hold globally. This is\nthe `FaddeevPhiStripGrowth.comparable` shape (upper + lower modulus bound) reduced to\nthe compact fundamental domain — the local Faddeev-asymptotic input that discharges\nthe global strip-growth axiom (off `phiBProd`'s zeros; divisor matching there is the\nseparate same-divisor input). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FaddeevStripGrowthBoxReduction.norm_le_of_periodic_ballBound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FaddeevStripGrowthBoxReduction.norm_le_of_periodic_ballBound","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FaddeevStripGrowthBoxReduction.lean#L49-L87","doc":"**A doubly-periodic function bounded on the fundamental ball is bounded\neverywhere.** If `r : ℂ → ℂ` is periodic under both vectors of an `ℝ`-basis `bas`\nof `ℂ`, and `‖r w‖ ≤ C` for every `w` in the closed ball of radius\n`‖bas 0‖ + ‖bas 1‖`, then `‖r z‖ ≤ C` for *all* `z`. Reducing the two `ℝ`-coordinates\nof `z` modulo `1` (`Int.fract`) lands `z`, up to a lattice translation `r` ignores, in\nthat ball. The non-holomorphic modulus-bound analogue of\n`const_of_doublyPeriodic`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}